---
description: ALHC Projects core conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

- `AGENTS.md` is the architecture source of truth; update it when the data model, auth flow, or layout changes.
- Keep the domain generic (Workspace → Project → Section → Task → Subtask, multi-homed tasks). Team workflows are built on top, never as schema.
- Every new table: RLS enabled, `deleted_at` for soft delete, no DELETE policy. Project-scoped tables use `<table>_<command>_<role>` policies via `has_project_role()` / `has_task_role()` (roles viewer < commenter < editor < admin < owner; `_own_<role>` for author/recipient-owned rows); only workspace-level tables use `_allowlisted`. Activity stories, inbox items, and project memberships are written only by triggers/RPCs; never grant clients insert on them.
- Reads go through `src/lib/data.ts` (always `deleted_at IS NULL`); writes go through Server Actions in `src/lib/actions.ts`.
- Task dates are `start_on` + `due_on` (start ≤ due). Only Timeline reads `start_on`; Calendar, filters, rules, and forms stay on `due_on`. Optional times live in `due_at` / `start_at` (+ `time_zone`); a trigger keeps the `_on` columns equal to their local date, so day-based code never reads the times.
- Recurrence (`tasks.recurrence`), dependencies (`task_dependencies`, via `add_task_dependency` / `remove_task_dependency`), and restore (`restore_task`) are database-enforced; the app mirrors them only for display (`src/lib/recurrence.ts`).
- Revoke EXECUTE from `public`, `anon`, and `authenticated` on every new SECURITY DEFINER function unless it is an intentional RPC (trigger functions included).
- Task filtering (views, dashboard widgets, Timeline) uses one config schema, evaluated by `filter_project_tasks` and mirrored in `src/lib/views.ts`; extend it rather than adding another filter format.
- Next.js 16: `proxy.ts` replaces middleware; `params`/`searchParams` are Promises. Check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using unfamiliar APIs.
- Before finishing: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, and `npm run db:test` for schema changes.
- Never commit secrets, service-role keys, or real allowlist emails. Never call the Asana API.
